From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:15:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] account: the id_token a game forwards to NEX is built and
 signed here, with the game token in its nnex claim

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Nextendo's integration guide names this the one thing a client must build for itself: a game never logs in
 with a password, it asks the system for a BAAS id_token and forwards it as its NEX login, and the server accepts the
 login only for the account the signed `nnex` claim proves. `LoadIdTokenCache` is that call (the reference client's
 `LoadIdTokenCache` in Ryujinx-Nextendo's ManagerServer.cs); the cut answer was a failure and the dauth chain's token
 is not what the server reads. Off unless `DM_NEXTENDO_NEX_TOKEN` is set, so every build without a game token is
 unchanged, and the signature comes from the Security framework with a generated key when no PEM is named.
Issue: https://github.com/GigiFrack/NX2Apple (fork)

